[0m  [2m-        "content": "The file `server.log` contains thousands of lines of server activity.\n\nExactly one line in that file records a successful order being placed.\nThat line contains an `ORDER_ID=...` token and a customer email.\n\nFind that line and write the answer as a two-line file named\n`answer.txt` in this directory, exactly in this format (no extra\nwhitespace, no quotes, no surrounding text):\n\n```\norder_id=<the ORDER_ID value>\ncustomer=<the customer email>\n```\n\nUse any tool you like \u2014 grep, Python, reading the file directly \u2014 but\nthe answer must be exact. There is only one matching line.\n\n\n<live-context>\n- Time: 2026-08-06 09:33:26 WIB (UTC+0700)\n- Git: main (Dirty (2443 changes))\n- Recent commits:\n  fd4f520d Restore challenge\n  508b33e6 Update with new experiment result (2.54.0)\n  f762ff89 Update experiment\n  aea4cac7 Re do experiment\n  1295eaf3 Fix the executive summary and the validators\n- Interactive: no \u2014 do not call AskUserQuestion, EnterPlanMode, or ExitPlanMode, and do not wait on user input mid-turn; there is no user to answer or approve a plan. Present any plan inline and proceed: decide based on the conversation and continue.\n</live-context>",
